# ============================================================================
# EYG TIRE & AUTO CARE — line endings and file modes
# ============================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# This repo is authored on Windows but built on Linux (Vercel). Without an
# explicit rule, Git records whatever the working copy has, so files get
# committed with CRLF and then checked out with CRLF on the build server. Two
# concrete failures follow:
#
#   1. Shebang scripts break. `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a valid interpreter line, and
#      the script fails with "no such file or directory" rather than anything
#      resembling a syntax error. That is a genuinely confusing morning.
#   2. Diffs go white. Every line differs by an invisible trailing \r, so a
#      one-line change reads as a whole-file rewrite and review becomes useless.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` says: normalise to LF in the repository, check out with LF
# everywhere. Windows handles LF in every editor it ships with, so nothing is
# lost by not checking out CRLF locally.
# ============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that must never be touched: line endings corrupt them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.avif   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.mp4    binary
*.webm   binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lockfiles: LF-only, and treated as text so Git can deduplicate the churn.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep the executable bit where it means something. Docker's entrypoint and any
# future bin/ script need it; Windows cannot represent the mode, so it must be
# set with `git update-index --chmod=+x <file>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf